  "name": "michaelbell-tinyqv",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "description": "TinyQV \u2014 a very small RISC-V SoC (RV32EC + Zcb + Zicond) optimized for minimum silicon area. It executes instructions nibble-serially from external QSPI Flash and uses QSPI PSRAM for data (no on-chip program memory), bundling UART, debug-UART, SPI, PWM, GPIO and a timer. Silicon-proven on the Tiny Tapeout 10 sky130 shuttle, with an SDK and example programs. Mirrored into the Vyges catalog as the minimum-area / commodity-memory RISC-V tier (below PicoRV32 / Ibex) for cost-sensitive mature-node SoCs. Upstream author: Michael Bell.",
